        <p>The Vásquez family built it to boil cochineal and indigo for the valley's weavers. One of their stone basins still stands in the courtyard, a fountain now, stained a faint red where the water used to run.</p>
        <p>A tailor cut suits in the front room from 1932, then the doors stayed shut for forty years. We restored it with masons from the barrio, keeping every beam we could save.</p>
